From 0b32546e073b150859230156ea81b8a9e763651b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenAI <noreply@openai.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 17:16:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tesla: harden precise stop and dynamic lead handling

Keep the existing gap table, persistence, asymmetric gap slew, and FCW constants intact, but close the real longitudinal gaps found after the recent Tesla tuning work:

* align the velocity-PID target with the same actuator horizon as aTarget; use a short kinematic target when experimental/e2e acceleration wins, and fall back to current speed rather than zero on an incomplete plan
* require persistent, continuous, low-speed lead motion plus closing-distance/braking-room guards before creep-follow can clear an ordinary lead0 stop; preserve e2e, leadTwo, cruise, external zero-speed, and force-decel stop requests, and let v_soft converge to a confirmed creeping lead's speed
* seed/reset the aLeadK derivative on first acquisition, radar/vision lead discontinuities, non-finite data, and solver reset; clip raw jerk and reset before set_weights so a cut-in cannot inherit the previous lead's relaxed jerk cost
* update the stale following-distance tests to the current 1.10-1.60s table and personality fallbacks, so CI verifies the code that is actually running

Add focused regression tests and update the tuning help text.
